Root cause:
The bug was caused by improper handling of socket connections in the HTTP push functionality, specifically related to the decrementing of the connection count and the logging of request completion. The patch addresses issues where the connection count was decremented even when the socket was not initialized, leading to potential underflow or incorrect connection tracking. Additionally, the logging of request completion was modified to ensure it only occurs when the socket is valid, preventing misleading logs for aborted requests.
